 "id": 31390,
 "title": "After I Took Her Place as the Crippled Wolf King's Bride, He Regretted It Forever",
 "slug": "after-i-took-her-place-as-the-crippled-wolf-kings-bride-he-regretted-it-forever",
 "platform": "miraluneshort",
 "episodes": 60,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/31390.webp",
 "description": "Vera Ashford has spent her life being overlooked in her own family. After her mother, Ida, dies under suspicious circumstances, Vera carries the Crimson Moon pendant and begins digging into the old case—and into the rescue she once performed, an identity her younger sister Delia stole and wore as her own. Cassian Thorne is the leader of the Northern Pack, crippled by an old silver-poison wound and confined to a wheelchair. He marries Vera in a cold, political arrangement—two guarded strangers testing each other across a marriage neither asked for. But as they dig side by side into Ida's death, suspicion gives way to trust, and trust to something warmer. Their investigation moves through fragments: the Crimson Moon pendant, an old recording, and shipping logs for a medicine chest that should never have existed. Each piece points toward Marcus and Selena, the figures who arranged the transport and then buried the evidence after the killing. Meanwhile, Leon Blackwood—the Eastern wolf Vera once loved—discovers the truth. She was the one who saved him, not Delia. The Silver Moon pendant Delia stole was his proof, and the lie collapses. Leon tries to win Vera back, but his apologies curdle into insistence, then into pursuit, crossing every line she draws. When Leon's pressure becomes a threat, Cassian rises from his wheelchair for the first time—not to fight, but to stand between Vera and the man who won't let go. Vera travels east to secure the physical evidence, and together she and Cassian expose Marcus and Selena's crimes before the packs. She refuses Leon's compensation and his pleas. She returns north, to the life she chose. A year later, Vera and Cassian hold a public wedding before the pack—no longer an arrangement, but a bond witnessed by the wolves who stood with them.",
 "about": "After I Took Her Place as the Crippled Wolf King's Bride, He Regretted It Forever is an English short drama in 60 episodes, originally released on MiraluneShort. It falls under Doctor & Medical, Werewolf & Alpha, Second Chance and Hidden Identity. Viewers on MiraluneShort rate it 8.5 out of 10. Every episode is free to watch on DramaDog, with no app or sign-up.",
