 "platform": "miraluneshort",
 "episodes": 60,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/31387.webp",
 "description": "Artist Emily and her fiancée, Becca, have been together for three years. But on their wedding day, Becca walks in arm in arm with wealthy heiress Cathy and announces that the ceremony is actually for the two of them. She even livestreams the humiliation. Becca snaps the necklace around Emily’s neck, while Cathy tears the skirt of her wedding gown. The livestream fills with comments mocking Emily as “a penniless artist nobody wants.” Just as security is about to drag Emily out, a commanding voice rings out from a corner. Sophia, head of the Brown Group, has just ended a phone call pressuring her to get married. Immediately drawn to the woman standing at the altar in a wedding dress, she slips a ring off her finger, drops to one knee, and proposes on the spot. Emily accepts. Becca and Cathy ridicule Sophia, dismissing her as a “poor driver.” Neither realizes she controls the country’s largest business conglomerate. Determined to succeed on her own merits, Emily refuses to rely on Sophia’s protection and insists on working her way up from the bottom. But trouble follows her. Gallery owner Jack pressures her to sleep with him and destroys her paintings. Cathy bribes Emily’s landlord to clear out her apartment, accuses her of plagiarism, and leaks her private photographs. Each time, Sophia steps in to fight back—smashing through the gallery doors, immediately terminating every business partnership with the Carter family, and exposing forged contracts at an art exhibition. Emily also defends herself, using timestamps on her artwork to prove her innocence and leaving Cathy’s younger brother, Reid, speechless when he is sent to intimidate her. Meanwhile, Becca drains Emily’s bank account, taking all her savings. Emily’s younger sister, Grace, is forced to leave school and has a bitter confrontation with her sister in the rain. Cathy then uses a dress and tuition money as leverage to pressure Grace into stealing their mother’s heirloom ring. Eventually, Grace breaks down at Sophia’s villa and confesses everything. The sisters reconcile. At the Brown Group’s year-end gala, Cathy hopes meeting the company’s president will help her turn her fortunes around. Instead, she discovers that the woman she mocked as a driver is the head of the Brown Group herself. Carter Capital is acquired outright, and Cathy and Becca are arrested at the banquet for forging contracts, illegally transferring funds, and violating Emily’s privacy. Sophia raises Emily’s hand and announces, “This is my wife—and a co-owner of the Brown Group.” One year later, Emily earns a promotion to Director of Art and Design through her own abilities, while Grace receives a full scholarship to the École des Beaux-Arts in Paris. Cathy and Becca are left to confront their regrets in prison. Emily and Sophia build a happy, fulfilling life together.",
