 "description": "\"The CEO's Secret Treatment: The Terminal Secretary's Rise\" Clara was the invisible secretary—deliberately plain, endlessly patient. Her colleagues mocked her, her mother drained her, and her stepfather Finn had been molesting her for years. Then came the diagnosis: terminal leukemia. Drunk and broken, she spent one reckless night with Dashiell, the company's CEO. When she woke, Clara tore off her disguise—and stunned everyone. She fought back against the coworkers who had tormented her and swore never to shrink herself again. Dashiell had been watching her long before that night. When he learned of her illness, he quietly assembled the world's top specialists and replaced her medication—hiding it all, protecting her from behind a wall of possessive tenderness. Her family kept dragging her down: her mother's endless demands, her stepfather's crimes. Clara gathered evidence and worked with her stepsister to put them both behind bars. When heiress Luci obsessed over Dashiell and attacked Clara again and again, he shut her down every time. What began as a drunken mistake and a short-term contract marriage deepened into something real. He finally confessed: he had known about her illness from the start and had been treating her in secret all along. Clara let go of her shame and her fear of death. Together they faced the pressure of an arranged marriage, family disasters, and workplace cruelty. Her leukemia was cured. Her past was buried. And their contract marriage became a real one. ——She thought she had no tomorrow. She didn't know someone had already built her a future.",
