 "description": "\"Dance of the Abyss\" Three years ago, Colton—an orphan—was adopted by Mark, a top-tier investor, and brought to Thorne Manor. The moment he laid eyes on his aloof, ethereal new brother Julian, he fell hopelessly, obsessively in love. Julian was once a celebrated dance prodigy, but years of manipulation and abuse at Mark's hands had left him broken—body and soul. Wary and bitter, he regarded this uninvited \"brother\" with nothing but contempt. What he didn't see was the blazing obsession burning behind Colton's gaze—an obsession that had already claimed Julian as its sole prey. To shatter Julian's last shred of pride, Mark announced the revival of Julian's magnum opus, The Abyss—and gave the lead role to Colton. Desperate and cornered, Julian had no choice but to approach Colton himself and agree to his forbidden terms. A deal sealed with flesh and blood dragged them both into a vortex from which there was no return. Colton appeared to be Mark's pawn, but in truth, every move he made was calculated to draw him closer to Julian. He quietly defied Mark's cruelty and guarded his wounded brother from the shadows. On the rehearsal floor, Julian taught Colton every step—and every touch, every shared spin on stage burned away the last of their restraint. When Julian's old injuries flared up, Colton's tender care made him feel cherished for the first time. And under Mark's relentless pressure, the two hearts only drew nearer. From resistance to surrender, from humiliation to devotion. When Mark threatened their future and demanded they earn double his investment, the brothers finally cast aside their differences and stood together. Colton swore that no one would ever hurt Julian again. And Julian, at last, let down his walls—and accepted this forbidden love. Together, they took the stage of The Abyss and shone with blinding brilliance—using their art to strike back at Mark, and finding in each other the redemption they had both been searching for. —\"I never wanted to escape the abyss. Because you were in it.\"",
