 "episodes": 60,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/29359.webp",
 "description": "In her past life, Eleanor, a wealthy heiress, was on a luxury cruise ship when her jealous roommate Vivian planted a virus to drain her bank account. In the end, Vivian pushed her into the sea, leaving her to die. Reborn right before the group boards the cruise for their trip, Eleanor swears to take revenge on her enemies. Vivian still plans to steal Eleanor’s fortune during the voyage. At the dock, she tries to borrow Eleanor’s phone to install the virus. Prepared, Eleanor lies that she left her smartphone at school and only carries a basic feature phone. Foiled, Vivian plants the virus on Sean’s phone instead and steals all his savings. Once aboard the cruise, Vivian puts on the act of a rich young lady, splurging wildly and treating everyone to a shopping spree at the luxury boutique for a total of 12 million. When the bill comes, she cannot pay. She makes excuse after excuse — claiming her card has a limit, accusing the store of selling counterfeit goods, and even fainting to escape. Eleanor exposes every lie. Sean, Chloe and Amy, who are traveling with them, are furious to find out Vivian is not wealthy, and a huge fight breaks out in the shop. Ethan, the cruise manager, arrives and recognizes Eleanor as the true heiress of the Vance family. Vivian, Sean and the others are caught red-handed. They are detained for vandalism and refusing to pay for the damages. Vivian gets bailed out only after Sean sells his house and takes out a high-interest loan. Sean remains clueless, still believing Vivian comes from a rich family. Back at university, Eleanor’s mother gifts her a custom sports car. Vivian and Sean show up to cause a scene. Sean destroys the car and calls thugs to threaten Eleanor. Isabella, the chairwoman of the Vance Group, arrives with her team, and all of Vivian’s lies crumble completely. In the end, Sean is sent to prison for intentional property damage. Vivian faces prosecution for theft and fraud. The Vance Group helps Sean’s parents resolve the loan-shark crisis, yet they will never pardon the wrongdoers. Having avenged her past self, Eleanor chooses not to take over the family business immediately. She decides to finish her studies and embrace a brand-new life.",
