 "description": "Elena Brooks has been married to Damian Walker for three years. For three years, he refused to have children—until one day he suddenly changed his mind and asked for a baby. Elena thought her dream had finally come true. During her pregnancy, her husband, her mother-in-law Margaret, and her best friend Vanessa surrounded her with care, nutrition plans, and devotion. She believed she was the luckiest woman alive. Then, days before her due date, she overheard the truth. Damian had been sleeping with Vanessa for years. Together they had a son—Noah—born with a severe heart condition. Elena was never a wife to them. She was an incubator. They had planned her pregnancy to harvest her unborn child's heart for Noah, and after the delivery, they intended to silence mother and child forever. Holding back contractions, Elena pretended to know nothing and waited for her chance. In the delivery ward, she broke free of her watchers, tore a bedsheet into a rope, and climbed out a window. She collapsed outside, bleeding, begging strangers for help—offering a hundred thousand dollars to anyone who would take her to another hospital. Damian caught her anyway. She was about to be sedated and restrained when two men walked in: Richard, chairman of the Carter Group, and his son Adrian. Richard had recognized the crescent-shaped birthmark on her wrist, run a DNA test, and confirmed it—Elena was his daughter, lost to him for twenty years. Protected by her father and brother, Elena gave birth safely and met the family she never knew she had. She ended the false marriage and became a Carter heiress. Damian, Vanessa, and Margaret kept pushing—using her position, the press, and the child as weapons. But Elena stopped hiding behind others. She took control of company affairs, gathered evidence, and struck back. In the end, the betrayers faced the law, and Elena rose as a leader of the Carter Group—with her son, and a life that finally belonged to her.",
