 "title": "THE KING FORGOT HIS LUNA. HIS WOLF DIDN'T",
 "slug": "the-king-forgot-his-luna-his-wolf-didnt",
 "platform": "yourchannel",
 "episodes": 50,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/28035.webp",
 "description": "He kissed her in front of seven kingdoms. Ten seconds later, he didn't know her name. Astrid is queen of the northern wolf kingdom, and the fated mate of Aldric, Alpha King of the South. On their wedding day his great black wolf walks up the aisle and kneels to her. Hundreds of wolves kneel with him. For one minute, she has everything. Then the dowager queen hands her stepson a cup of wine. The poison has a name: forget-wife. Aldric wakes with a stranger's face beside him and roars that omega trash has been let into his throne room. He tears the snow-silver crown off her head and breaks it on the steps. He strips her title, her rooms, her name, and makes her pour wine for his new favorite in the ashes of her wedding. But the poison has rules, and the dowager recites them smiling. One. He no longer knows his mate. Two. His wolf still loves her. Three. Every step that wolf takes toward her, a black mark crawls one inch closer to his heart. Five full moons. Then he dies. So the only way to keep her husband alive is to make his wolf hate her. The one creature still faithful to her, she must drive away with stones and a whip, in public, while the court laughs. She spits \"I don't know this wolf.\" She kneels. She bleeds. She never explains why. Because if she whistles, if she lets his wolf choose her, she kills the man she is saving. And every night the king still comes to her door, dragged there by a beast he can't control, furious at a woman he can't stop wanting, the black mark climbing toward his heart. He hates her. His body does not. That is the whole trap. The antidote exists in one place: the hands of the Raven Emperor, across a war. To buy it she must trade her own wolf, Hela, as a hostage, and every mile between them cuts her open. She is exiled, flogged, annulled, sentenced to hang, hunted across the snow. Through all of it, the countdown climbs. The fifth full moon comes with her head on an execution block and seven kingdoms watching. The dowager has already won. Then the king's wolf walks onto the scaffold, past two hundred guards, past the executioner, past its dying master, and takes her side. It carries the cure in its teeth. It puts it in the king's mouth. The mark recedes. The king opens his eyes and says her name. And the queen does the one thing she has been forbidden for five moons: she whistles. A wolf that belongs to a king kneels to a woman with no wolf of her own. She merges with him. Her hair turns white, gold fur breaks through her skin, and a wolf's shadow rises to the dome. Two hundred black-armored wolves hit the floor. \"Ravenna. Kneel.\" The dowager's own wolf lies down at her feet. But a crown taken back is not a marriage healed. The man who forgot her must live with what he did. The woman who saved him is not ready to forgive an hour of it. The war that sold the poison is already at the northern gate. She saved his life by breaking his heart. Now she has to decide whether to give it back.",
 "about": "THE KING FORGOT HIS LUNA. HIS WOLF DIDN'T is an English short drama in 50 episodes, originally released on YourChannel in November 2026. It falls under Forbidden Love, Werewolf & Alpha, Royalty & Palace and Underdog Rise. Viewers on YourChannel rate it 7.8 out of 10. Every episode is free to watch on DramaDog, with no app or sign-up.",
