 "description": "\"Charlie lost his brother to Rachel's father. He lost everything else to revenge. He made Rachel's family bankrupt, killed her father, forced her to donate bone marrow to his fake girlfriend, and watched her lose their unborn child. Then she jumped off the Brooklyn Bridge and was gone. Three years later, Charlie found her in a Texas trailer park — alive, but with no memory of him or their past. Her mind was stuck at five years old. He begged to stay. He tried to atone. He fixed roofs, rescued her cat, took beatings from her protector. But when her memory finally returned, so did all the pain. She was dying. Organ failure. No cure. She ran from Manhattan one last time — to a hospice on Long Island. Charlie chased her. At the door, her friend blocked him. She died alone, in a room where he couldn't reach her. Charlie lost everything — his money, his power, his mind. He made things right with the people he hurt. Then on a rainy night, at her grave, he ended his own life. They started with love. They ended with nothing but blood and rain.\"",
