 "description": "Isabella, the Queen of the Nightveil, sealed her royal power and masked her pheromones for a love she once believed was worth it. She married Damon, a Beta, living as a “wolfless nobody” and spending ten years as his housewife. Three times, she pulled his failing company back from the brink of bankruptcy and secured him an exclusive spot at the Royal Academy — yet she never revealed where the funds and opportunities truly came from. Her royal seal and classified documents lay on the study desk all along, but Damon never once bothered to open that door in a decade. On the night of their tenth-anniversary gala, he handed her official invitation to the doorman and said only, “I don’t know her. This is my wife,” before walking the red carpet arm-in-arm with Vivian. Their son Leo publicly called Vivian “Mommy,” while Isabella was blocked at the steps. She did not scream or weep. She slipped off her ring, dropped it on the ground, and climbed into a black sedan. Turning to Marcus, she said, “I’m ready to restore my identity. And I want everything I gave Damon back.” He never thought she would leave for good. He assumed it was just a petty tantrum, that once her money ran out, she would come back to the kitchen. But partnerships dissolved, key projects were withdrawn, and his accounts froze. He lost three major deals one after another. His company collapsed, his property went to auction. He burned down the kitchen by accident, and Leo was hospitalized from food poisoning — yet he still waited for the “housewife” who would calm down and return. Vivian stole his plans and pocketed kickbacks. When she tried to interview before the Senate, security dragged her out of the elevator. Meanwhile, Isabella sat at the head of the conference table and ordered, “Terminate her employment and blacklist her across all industries,” shutting every door for Vivian. Even then, Damon insisted his wife had attached herself to an elder. He stormed into the Senate chamber shouting, waving a crumpled marriage certificate and demanding compensation, only to be dragged away by Marcus time and again. It was the Royal Academy’s notice — “This enrollment privilege belongs to Ms. Isabella” — that planted the first seed of doubt. Back home, he found an old silk scarf tucked inside the box marked as their first-anniversary gift. Royal pheromones exploded forth the second he touched it, and he collapsed to his knees, shaking uncontrollably. That same day, an envoy of the Blood Moon arrived with an invitation and told him plainly: she was the Queen of the Nightveil. In court, every document Damon presented bore his own signature. Vivian turned on him, sneering, “You signed them willingly.” The divorce was finalized. She fled with cash and jewels, only to be arrested at the airport. Damon moved into a rental house with Leo and took work hauling cement at a construction site. He looked up at a mall billboard showing the Blood Moon Wolf King bowing to kiss Isabella’s hand and whispered, “That used to be my wife.” The cement sack slipped and crashed at his feet. Leo had learned to sign papers on his own and said softly, “Mom doesn’t seem to need us anymore.” Inside the royal hall, Marcus held out the crown. Isabella placed it upon her head and ascended the throne as every noble bowed low. She was no longer the wife turned away at the gala steps. Their two worlds were separated forever.",
