 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/31414.webp",
 "description": "Three years ago, Liam was the beloved Rayne cherished in the palm of his hand. Until an anonymous tip and a piece of bloody surveillance footage made Liam firmly believe that Rayne was the culprit who had massacred his elder brother. In the most passionate moment of intimacy, the sweet scent of pheromones masked the intent to kill, and Liam drove a dagger hard into Rayne’s heart. That stab not only nearly cost Rayne his life, but also completely stripped him of power, deprived him of his inheritance rights, and exiled him to this hell on earth. Now, their positions were reversed. The sealed, despairing Blackthorn Island became Rayne’s perfect theater of revenge. He wanted to torment him, yet could not control his attraction to him; he crushed Liam with absolute power and built the strongest cage with pheromones. And Liam silently endured all the humiliation and plunder—because his true purpose in entering prison was to find the last traces of his brother Nolan. In this power game reeking of blood, the two were repeatedly torn between “hating each other to the bone” and “loving each other and wanting each other to live.” Every clash was a deep kiss laced with glass shards. During a prison riot, Liam was seriously injured. While rescuing him, Rayne was shocked to discover a strange old wound near Liam’s ribs—a metal capsule that Liam had cut open his own flesh and sewn into his body! When the capsule was decoded, the conspiracy from three years ago came crashing down like cold water: the mastermind behind the massacre of Liam’s brother, the fabrication of evidence, and the plot to kill Rayne by using another’s blade was actually the exalted First Prince Cassius. The misunderstanding was torn apart, and the former lovers stood amid the ruins, covered in blood. There was no hesitant mutual confession of feelings—only a last-stand counterattack intertwined with blood and bone. Rayne leveraged the vilest forces of Blackthorn Island, Liam transformed into the sharpest blade, and the two former sworn enemies and former lovers fought with their backs to the wall. Together they set off a prison break and rebellion that swept across the entire star system, aiming their guns directly at the throne of the imperial capital. In the end, the First Prince’s ambition was reduced to ashes amid the gunfire, and atop this ruin, the dawn that belonged to them arrived.",
 "about": "Trapped by the Alpha I “Killed” is an English short drama in 59 episodes, originally released on MiraluneShort. It falls under System, Werewolf & Alpha, Heir & Heiress and Revenge. Viewers on MiraluneShort rate it 8.7 out of 10. Every episode is free to watch on DramaDog, with no app or sign-up.",
