 "episodes": 60,
 "cover": "https://dramadog.app/c/31410.webp",
 "description": "Jack, the owner of a fishing company, was conspired against by his ex-wife Diana and her lover Marcus, who transferred all his assets and left him with nothing. He returned with his eight-year-old daughter Lily to his hometown of Greyhaven and moved into the dilapidated house his father had left him. On the day he returned, he was beaten and kicked by relatives who refused to pay what they owed him, and then he received a final notice to pay $5,000 in property tax within 15 days. In desperation, he touched his father’s relic and awakened his Atlantean bloodline—he could breathe underwater and sense schools of fish and the seafloor terrain. He met Bella, the daughter of an old fisherman. Bella had a fishing license but no boat, while Jack had a boat but no license, so they teamed up. Relying on his sea sense, Jack turned his fortune around by recovering bluefin tuna from the seabed and gold coins from a pirate ship, defeating Rex, Victor, Lucas, Glenn the Crab King, and the Shark Pirates one after another. Eventually, during the Alaskan king crab season, he drove Marcus and Diana bankrupt and sent them to prison. He used the trident to activate Lily’s bloodline and cure her leukemia, bought back his company and villa, married Bella, and became the true “King of the Deep.”",
 "about": "My Ex Took Everything. Now I Own the Sea. is an English short drama in 60 episodes, originally released on MiraluneShort. It falls under Divorce & Exes, Marriage & Wedding and Romance. Viewers on MiraluneShort rate it 8.4 out of 10. Every episode is free to watch on DramaDog, with no app or sign-up.",
